body: |-
  ## Files created
  - packages/paradigm-mcp/src/tools/propose-block.ts (paradigm_propose_block tool)
  - packages/paradigm-mcp/src/tools/authority.ts (paradigm_authority_claim + paradigm_authority_release tools, self-contained YAML I/O)
  - packages/paradigm/src/commands/internal/active-remediations.ts (helper backing `paradigm internal active-remediations --json`)
  - packages/paradigm/src/commands/internal/.purpose
  - .paradigm/remediations/.gitkeep + .paradigm/remediations/.archived/.gitkeep

  ## Files modified
  - packages/paradigm/src/core/authority.ts (+85 lines, 4 reader/mutator functions)
  - packages/paradigm/src/core/authority.test.ts (+ tests for readers)
  - packages/paradigm-mcp/src/tools/index.ts (registered authority + propose-block as feature tier)
  - packages/paradigm-mcp/src/tools/.purpose (3 new symbols)
  - packages/paradigm/src/__tests__/integration-build.test.ts (vitest timeout 5s → 60s; bundle grew with v6.1 Wave 1)

  ## Build status
  - paradigm-mcp build: clean
  - paradigm build + link: clean
  - vitest: 320 pass / 1 skip (delta +7 from 313 baseline)

  ## Wave 2 prerequisites
  - HAS_ACTIVE_REMEDIATION helper near line 85 of paradigm-common.sh (see spec §1.7)
  - Check 14 (remediation-gate) appended after Check 13
  - PARADIGM_OVERRIDE env var branch with overrides.jsonl writer
  - Regenerate mirrors via node scripts/generate-hooks.mjs

  ## Key design choice: self-contained YAML I/O in authority MCP tool
  paradigm-mcp does NOT depend on @a-company/paradigm directly (no entry in package.json deps). Spec §7 said "consume reader/writer from core/authority.ts" but that would require a cross-package dep that creates a cycle. Pragmatic call: authority MCP tool re-implements minimal read/write (~30 lines) using js-yaml. paradigm/src/core/authority.ts readers are still authoritative for the CLI side (paradigm shift, Wave 3 paradigm override).

  ## Rate-limit recovery note
  Background Builder hit org monthly usage limit at ~20 tool uses. Main session resumed: read partial state via git status, completed remaining files manually. No data loss. Faster than re-firing.
